        "explanation": "Semantic Versioning (SemVer) is a universal standard for versioning software. A version number consists of three parts: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (e.g., `1.4.2`).\n1. **MAJOR:** Breaking changes (incompatible API changes).\n2. **MINOR:** New features added in a backward-compatible manner.\n3. **PATCH:** Backward-compatible bug fixes.",
