        "title": "How do you organize routes in large applications?",
        "category": "2. Intermediate Level (51–100) - Express.js & REST APIs",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "In large applications, putting all routes in `server.js` creates a massive, unmaintainable file. Instead, you use the MVC (Model-View-Controller) architecture along with `express.Router()`. \n1. **Routes Folder:** Maps URLs to specific Controller functions.\n2. **Controllers Folder:** Contains the actual business logic for the route.\n3. **Models Folder:** Contains the database schemas.",
