        "tip": "Returning accurate status codes is vital for frontend developers. A frontend library (like Axios) relies entirely on the status code to decide whether to trigger the `then()` block or the `catch()` block.",
        "mistake": "Always returning `200 OK`, even when an error occurs, but putting `{ \"error\": true }` in the JSON body. This breaks standard HTTP tooling.",
        "summary": "Standardized 3-digit responses from a server indicating the outcome of a request, categorized into informational, success, redirection, client error, and server error groups."
