        "id": 69,
        "title": "What is response object?",
        "category": "2. Intermediate Level (51–100) - Express.js & REST APIs",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "The Response object (`res`) represents the HTTP response that the Express server will send back to the client. It provides methods to format data, set HTTP headers, specify status codes, and ultimately end the request-response cycle.",
