        "title": "What is CORS?",
        "category": "2. Intermediate Level (51–100) - Express.js & REST APIs",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) is a security mechanism enforced by web browsers. By default, a web application running on one origin (e.g., `http://localhost:3000`) is prohibited from making API requests to a different origin (e.g., `http://api.mybackend.com:8080`). CORS allows the server to specify exactly which origins are allowed to access its resources.",
