        "category": "3. Experienced / Advanced Level (101–150) - Event Loop & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "The `EventEmitter` is a core class in Node.js (from the `events` module) that facilitates event-driven programming. It allows objects to emit named events that cause previously registered 'listener' functions to be called synchronously in the order they were registered.",
