        "title": "How does EventEmitter work internally?",
        "category": "3. Experienced / Advanced Level (101–150) - Event Loop & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "Internally, an `EventEmitter` maintains an object (a hash map) where the keys are the event names (Strings), and the values are Arrays of listener functions. When `.emit('eventName')` is called, it looks up the key in the object and loops through the array, executing every function synchronously.",
