        "code": "# 1. Use lightweight Node 20 image\nFROM node:20-alpine\n\n# 2. Create app directory inside container\nWORKDIR /usr/src/app\n\n# 3. Copy package.json FIRST (Crucial for caching)\nCOPY package*.json ./\n\n# 4. Install dependencies\nRUN npm install --production\n\n# 5. Copy the rest of the source code\nCOPY . .\n\n# 6. Expose the port\nEXPOSE 3000\n\n# 7. Start the app\nCMD [\"node\", \"server.js\"]",
        "tip": "Notice that we copy `package.json` and run `npm install` BEFORE copying the rest of the code. This is an advanced technique. Docker caches each step. If you only change a line of code in `server.js`, Docker skips the slow `npm install` step entirely!",
        "mistake": "Forgetting to add a `.dockerignore` file (which should include `node_modules`). If you don't, Docker will slowly copy your massive local `node_modules` folder into the container.",
