        "tip": "Preflight requests can double your API latency because it requires two full network round-trips. You can tell the browser to cache the preflight approval by setting the `Access-Control-Max-Age` header.",
        "mistake": "Freaking out when you see an `OPTIONS` request failing in the network tab and thinking your API route is broken. Your API is fine; your CORS configuration is broken.",
        "summary": "An automatic `OPTIONS` request sent by the browser before a complex cross-origin request to verify if the server permits the impending action."
