        "category": "4. Bonus Questions (151–225) - Real-Time, DevOps & Testing",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) is a security header sent by the server. It tells the browser: 'For the next X months, NEVER try to load this website using insecure HTTP. Always force HTTPS.' It protects users from man-in-the-middle attacks, especially on public Wi-Fi.",
        "example": "Setting the header.",
