        "tip": "If a user manually types `http://yourbank.com`, without HSTS, the initial request goes over insecure HTTP before the server redirects them to HTTPS. A hacker can intercept that very first insecure request.",
        "mistake": "Adding HSTS to `localhost` during development. It will break your local environment because you rarely have an SSL certificate locally.",
        "summary": "An HTTP header that commands the browser to exclusively communicate with the server over secure HTTPS connections, preventing downgrade attacks."
