        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "The Singleton Pattern ensures that a class has only one instance globally and provides a single point of access to it. In Node.js, because of the way the `require()` caching mechanism works, every module you export is inherently evaluated as a Singleton.",
        "example": "Node.js caching magic.",
