        "category": "4. Bonus Questions (151–225) - Real-Time, DevOps & Testing",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "A 'Cold Start' occurs when a Serverless function (like AWS Lambda) is invoked after being idle for a period of time. Because AWS destroyed the container to save resources, it must provision a new container, load the Node.js runtime, and execute the initialization code before it can process the request. This can cause the first user's request to take 1-3 seconds instead of 50 milliseconds.",
        "example": "The lifecycle.",
