        "tip": "To prevent Cold Starts, companies use 'Provisioned Concurrency' (paying AWS to keep a few containers permanently warm) or run 'ping' scripts that hit the API every 5 minutes to keep it awake.",
        "mistake": "Connecting to the database *inside* the route handler. Always establish DB connections *outside* the handler so they can be reused during Warm Starts.",
        "summary": "The latency delay experienced on the first execution of a serverless function because the cloud provider must provision a fresh container and boot the Node.js runtime."
